<title>CAMEROON: Cameroon names coffee/cocoa quality checkers.</title>
<headline>Cameroon names coffee/cocoa quality checkers.</headline>
<dateline>YAOUNDE 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cameroon has named three firms to inspect cocoa and coffee exports from August 1997 to raise the quality of beans reaching world markets, a government source said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Swiss firm Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS), Dutch firm Cornelder and Cameroon's Observatoire Camerounais de Qualite would monitor quality from the start of Cameroon's 1997/98 cocoa season on Friday, August 1, the source said.</p>
<p>Cameroon expects to produce 130,000 tonnes of cocoa in 1997/98, he added.</p>
<p>Cameroon closed its Office Nationale de Commercialisation des Produits de Base in 1989. Both products have been subject to discounts on world markets in recent years.</p>
<p>Cameroon has put the problem down to a boom in the number of inexperienced buyers and exporters after donor-sponsored liberalisation of marketing in the early 1990s.</p>
<p>-- Abidjan newsroom, +225 21 90 90</p>
